---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PolicyNote from '../components/PolicyNote.astro';
import policies from '../data/policy-updates.json';
import '../styles/learning.css';
---
<Base title="What's changed in Australian money rules?" description="Understand changes to Australian home-buyer support, property tax and foreign-buyer rules. See who is affected, when changes apply and the official sources.">
<header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap lesson-header"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Rule updates</div><h1>What's changed?</h1><p>The change. Who it affects. What to check next.</p></header>
<div class="hl-wrap lesson-shell"><p class="hl-help">A proposal is not a law. A passed law may start later. Status is based on the dated source check, not a live legal service.</p>
<section class="hl-content"><h2><time datetime="2026-10-17">17 October 2026</time> — inspectable money experiments</h2><p>Published three <a href="/worked-examples/">original worked investigations</a>: bill timing and same-day risk, comparing salary packages on equal terms, and the order of missed savings bonuses. Added downloadable default inputs/results and a 91-day CSV ledger. These are constructed educational scenarios, not customer records. This release does not update financial-rule review dates or bank snapshots.</p></section>
{policies.map(p=><PolicyNote id={p.id} full/>)}
<section class="lesson-more" id="site-corrections" aria-labelledby="site-corrections-title">
  <h2 id="site-corrections-title">Site corrections &amp; improvements</h2>
  <p><strong><time datetime="2026-10-16">16 October 2026</time> — a clearer workspace for money decisions</strong></p><p>Rebuilt the home page with direct tool links and an adjustable savings example using the existing calculation engine. Added a searchable tool directory and an in-page comparison of two salary offers. Updated shared navigation, reading layouts and mobile forms. The free payday planner is labelled as a finished free tool. Separately rechecked the cited ATO, Moneysmart and enacted-reform sources for the capital-gains-tax and negative-gearing guides. Updated the CGT source links and clarified that the future rule refers to gains accruing from its commencement date. Only those two guide checks and the CGT reform check were renewed; other guide and bank-data dates are unchanged.</p>
  <p><strong><time datetime="2026-10-12">12 October 2026</time> — A simpler payday planner and targeted source checks</strong></p>
  <p>The home page now starts with the payday planner. Empty plans show an input prompt, edited examples keep their example label, and successful calculations move to the result. Existing tools remain available as secondary resources. Rechecked the listed sources for the first-home deposit, stamp-duty and foreign-buyer guides; other guide dates are unchanged.</p>
  <p>Added the <a href="/methodology/#cash-flow">daily cash-flow formulas, cents handling and calendar assumptions</a> for the free planner. Rechecked the cited sources for the four rule summaries above: the first-home deposit scheme, future CGT and rental-loss reforms, and established-home foreign-investment restrictions. Their headline summaries remain unchanged. This targeted check does not renew every source date in the linked lessons.</p>
  <p><strong><time datetime="2026-10-06">6 October 2026</time> — Bank calculations, publisher description and planner clarity</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Corrected the <a href="/calculators/compound-interest/">bank-rate picker</a> so ambiguous total-rate rows, prose-only caps and expiry periods cannot produce unsupported combined projections. Account balance limits apply to the whole plan. Saved bank rates require fresh supported data or a newly entered custom rate.</li>
    <li>Excluded explicit business-only and SMSF-only products from the general personal savings comparison. Corrected shared tier-boundary handling and very-small-rate arithmetic in the savings-goal and mortgage engines.</li>
    <li>Made two targeted corrections to the <a href="/guides/apply-for-an-australian-tfn/">archived TFN guide</a>: lawful TFN recipients and eligibility for the Services Australia application route. This was not a fresh review of every archived instruction.</li>
    <li>Corrected the <a href="/about/#publisher">publisher description</a> by removing an unsupported educational-qualification claim. Howloop does not claim financial-adviser or tax-agent registration.</li>
    <li>Added a reproducible <a href="/tools/cash-flow/#worked-example">payday and bills example</a> with every starting input. It shows how a positive 13-week finish can still hide an earlier cash shortfall. The figures use the planner's existing calculation engine.</li>
    <li>Made the free planner easier to find in the tool directory and navigation. Guide search now supports multiple words and announces its results; the complete library remains readable without JavaScript.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These are website and explanation changes. They do not advance the financial-rule source-check dates or bank-data retrieval dates shown elsewhere.</p>
</section>
<section class="hl-content"><h2><time datetime="2026-10-16">16 October 2026</time> — clearer navigation and corrected explanations</h2><p>Simplified the homepage around pay, savings and bill timing; restored the all-tools directory and working language routes. Removed a separate homepage pay calculation whose static and interactive figures disagreed, and removed repeated tax text from tool pages. The salary tool continues to use the published PAYG schedules.</p><p>Corrected the methodology to describe monthly mortgage modelling and payroll withholding. Removed unsupported personal-author and verification claims, restored the publisher’s AI-assistance and review disclosures, and aligned the privacy policy with optional saves, analytics, hosting measurement and the optional AI question service. Ownership verification remains present; ad serving is disabled in this release. These content and navigation corrections do not advance the financial-rule source-check dates or bank-data retrieval dates.</p></section>
<details class="lesson-more"><summary>Earlier site updates &amp; how corrections work</summary><p><strong>18 September 2026 — usability and content review:</strong> Expanded all eight shorter money lessons with worked examples. Improved amount formatting and total mortgage-payment labels; added explicit base-versus-conditional bank scenarios with welcome-period expiry. Tax preparation now supports optional saving, restoring and clearing on this device. Aligned page addresses and sitemaps, and updated the privacy notice to describe the deployed Cloudflare traffic beacon.</p><p><strong>18 September 2026:</strong> Added eight beginner lessons, an LVR calculator, source-review dates and a rule-change record. Lessons start with an example and a quick check; detailed explanations remain available below.</p><div class="hl-content"><section><h2><time datetime="2026-09-18">18 September 2026</time> — Employee tax return companion</h2><p>Added a <a href="/tax-return">three-step preparation guide</a> with income-year and coverage checks, occupation sources, record reminders, six expense topics, a local expense organiser and downloadable CSV and myTax checklists. Expense arithmetic separates private use and work-use reimbursements; it does not assess tax deductibility. It does not decide deductions, estimate refunds or lodge returns. The guided flow runs without AI; optional AI explanations are disabled until separately configured.</p></section><section><h2><time datetime="2026-09-18">18 September 2026</time> — Australian money tools</h2><ul><li>Introduced compound-interest, mortgage and offset, savings-goal and emergency-fund calculators with assumptions and calculation breakdowns.</li><li>Published the bank explorer with dated public CDR product snapshots. Missing or partial data is labelled. Supported base rates are modelled separately from bonus and introductory components.</li><li>Expanded six money guides with worked comparisons, common mistakes and primary-source references.</li><li>Added a starting-point guide, topic navigation and individual article update records.</li><li>Separated older everyday how-to guides into a labelled archive. Their existing URLs remain available; they are outside the current money-guide library.</li></ul><p><a href="/methodology">Calculation and data methods →</a></p></section><section><h2>How a correction is handled</h2><p>Send the page URL, the part that seems wrong and a source or reproducible example to the address on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Use sample amounts and leave out account identifiers.</p><p>A verified error in a formula, example or explanation is corrected in the affected page. A material change should be recorded here or in the article's update note. Typographical or layout changes do not need to be presented as a new factual review.</p></section><section><h2>What an update date means</h2><p>A guide's publication date records when it first appeared. Its update date records a material edit; a source-check date records a check of its cited references. Bank retrieval dates describe a separate data snapshot and cannot guarantee a current offer. None of these dates means a licensed adviser has reviewed the page.</p></section><p><a href="/editorial-policy">Read the publishing policy →</a></p></div></details>
</div></Base>